{"name":"Grand Casino Gold","hex":"#edcd62","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grand","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Large, senior (high-ranking), intense, extreme, or exceptional\nOf a large size or extent; great.","Of a large size or extent; great."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thousand of some unit of currency, such as dollars or pounds.","A thousand RPM."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grand"},{"term":"casino","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A public building or room for gambling.","A small house; a pleasure house or holiday home, especially in Italy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/casino"},{"term":"gold","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A heavy yellow elemental metal of great value, with atomic number 79.","A coin or coinage made of this material, or supposedly so."]},{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["☉ (alchemy)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gold"}],"entries":[{"title":"Casino","blocks":[{"text":"A casino is a facility for gambling. Casinos are often built near or combined with hotels, resorts, restaurants, retail shopping, cruise ships, and other tourist attractions. Some casinos are also known for hosting live entertainment, such as stand-up comedy, concerts, and sporting events. The term casino is of Italian origin, from the root word casa meaning \"house.\" Originally, the term referred to a small country villa, summerhouse, or social club. During the 19th century, casino came to encompass other public buildings where pleasurable activities took place."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Caesars_Palace_Casino_%287980362756%29.jpg/330px-Caesars_Palace_Casino_%287980362756%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Casino","wikidata":"Q133215"},{"title":"Gold","blocks":[{"text":"Gold is a chemical element; its chemical symbol is Au and atomic number 79. In its pure form, it is a bright-metallic-yellow, dense, soft, malleable, and ductile metal. Chemically, gold is a transition metal, a group 11 element, and one of the noble metals. It is one of the least reactive chemical elements, being the second lowest in the reactivity series, with only platinum ranked as less reactive. Gold is solid under standard conditions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Gold-crystals.jpg/330px-Gold-crystals.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold","wikidata":"Q897"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/%22Orient_Saloon_at_Bisbee%2C_Arizona..._Faro_game_in_full_blast._Recognized%2C_Left_to_right-Tony_Downs_%28standing_with_derby%29_-_NARA_-_530986.jpg/500px-%22Orient_Saloon_at_Bisbee%2C_Arizona..._Faro_game_in_full_blast._Recognized%2C_Left_to_right-Tony_Downs_%28standing_with_derby%29_-_NARA_-_530986.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/%22Orient_Saloon_at_Bisbee%2C_Arizona..._Faro_game_in_full_blast._Recognized%2C_Left_to_right-Tony_Downs_%28standing_with_derby%29_-_NARA_-_530986.jpg/1280px-%22Orient_Saloon_at_Bisbee%2C_Arizona..._Faro_game_in_full_blast._Recognized%2C_Left_to_right-Tony_Downs_%28standing_with_derby%29_-_NARA_-_530986.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/%22Orient_Saloon